WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.707
Week 1 in one paragraph.

2
00:00:01.987 --> 00:00:14.317
Put the model call on your server, and pick the request shape from the task: synchronous for short machine-facing work, streaming for a person watching, background jobs for long work, batch for work that can wait.

3
00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:27.525
Classify failures, retry only transient ones at one layer with jittered backoff inside a deadline, break circuits on dead dependencies, fall back to models whose quality you’ve measured, and degrade on purpose.

4
00:00:27.805 --> 00:00:41.160
Deploy where the platform’s limits contain your deadlines with room to spare, keep secrets in secret stores and out of browsers, separate environments down to the API key, and gate every release on checks a machine runs.

5
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.328
Next week is about making all of this cheaper and faster: caching, batching, routing, and budgets.
